    "['remote-ip [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ldp interface lo0.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]', 'unit [parameter2] family [parameter3] [parameter4] [parameter5]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols ldp interface lo0.0\\nset protocols ldp neighbor 1.1.1.9\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, LDP neighbors are typically configured under `protocols ldp` hierarchy\\n- The `remote-ip 1.1.1.9` from Huawei specifies an LDP remote peer, which translates to an LDP neighbor configuration in Juniper\\n- Juniper requires specifying the local interface (usually lo0.0) for LDP along with neighbor statements\\n- The neighbor IP (1.1.1.9) is directly specified in the neighbor statement', 'trans_template': 'set protocols ldp interface lo0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ldp neighbor 1.1.1.9', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]', 'unit [parameter2] family [parameter3] [parameter4] [parameter5]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols ldp interface lo0.0\\nset protocols ldp neighbor 1.1.1.9\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, LDP neighbors are typically configured under `protocols ldp` hierarchy\\n- The `remote-ip 1.1.1.9` from Huawei specifies an LDP remote peer, which translates to an LDP neighbor configuration in Juniper\\n- Juniper requires specifying the local interface (usually lo0.0) for LDP along with neighbor statements\\n- The neighbor IP (1.1.1.9) is directly specified in the neighbor statement', 'trans_template': 'set protocols ldp neighbor 1.1.1.9'}]]": 1,
