    "['destination [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path LSP-to-1.1.1.9 to 1.1.1.9', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Huawei `destination 1.1.1.9` command for an MPLS TE tunnel:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols mpls label-switched-path LSP-to-1.1.1.9 to 1.1.1.9\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, MPLS TE tunnels are configured as Label Switched Paths (LSPs), and the `to` statement specifies the destination address, which is equivalent to Huawei\\'s `destination` command in the tunnel interface context. The LSP name is arbitrary (I used \"LSP-to-1.1.1.9\" as an example), but should match whatever naming convention you\\'re using in the Juniper configuration.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path LSP-to-1.1.1.9 to 1.1.1.9'}]]": 1,
