    "['mpls te tunnel-id [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10-to-1.1.1.9 tunnel-id 101', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10-to-1.1.1.9 tunnel-id 101\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, MPLS TE tunnels are configured as label-switched paths (LSPs). The equivalent command creates an LSP with the specified tunnel ID. The naming convention \"Tunnel10-to-1.1.1.9\" follows Juniper\\'s typical pattern of \"[interface]-to-[destination]\". The actual name can vary based on network design preferences.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10-to-1.1.1.9 tunnel-id 101'}]]": 1,
